+V3 captures immutable primitive pin/manifest digests at initial admission. Its
+post-run check rejects changed pin bytes first, then reads the manifest once
+and checks that same buffer against the captured digest **before** parsing or
+following any rows. It does not take expected digests from the returned mutable
+report or pin buffer. Frozen-file checks use a private copy of the row list.
+Seven additional tests use only owned scratch files: unchanged seal, changed
+listed bytes, a replacement manifest plus matching replacement file, changed
+invalid JSON, changed missing-path rows, pin tamper precedence, and mutation of
+returned report/pin buffers. They establish this seal behavior without a real
+artifact-admission success or any packet/engine mutation.
